  "aoi_source": "31 deg 04' 56.41\" N, 98 deg 42' 17.98\" E -- right bank of the Jinsha River, Jiangda County, Tibet Autonomous Region, on the Tibet-Sichuan border. Two successive landslide dams, 2018-10-10 and 2018-11-03; the second impounded a lake reported at 105e6 m^3, released through an engineered channel on 2018-11-13. Sources (see docs/validation.md 2.2): \"Study on successive landslide damming events of Jinsha River in Baige village on October 11 and November 3, 2018\", Journal of Engineering Geology; \"Hydro-sediment-morphodynamic processes of the Baige landslide-induced barrier lake, Jinsha River, China\", Journal of Hydrology; \"Using a single remote-sensing image to calculate the height of a landslide dam and the maximum volume of a lake\", NHESS 22, 2081-2098, 2022. Published volume figures CONFLICT across sources (105 vs 500 vs 775 e6 m^3) and must be quoted as a range, never as a single number.",
